   "s": "IDFCFIRSTB",
   "n": "IDFC First Bank Limited",
   "cat": "Outcome of Board Meeting",
   "when": "2026-10-24 17:30",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**\nThe Board approved key leadership and board transitions:\n* **Appointment of Mr. S. Ganesh Kumar** as Part-Time Non-Executive Chairperson w.e.f. May 10, 2027 to April 29, 2029 (succeeding Mr. Sanjeeb Chaudhuri whose term ends May 9, 2027), subject to RBI approval.\n* **Re-appointment of Mr. Pradeep Natarajan** as Whole-Time Director (Executive Director) for a 3-year term from June 1, 2027 to May 31, 2030, subject to RBI approval.\n* **Cessation of Mr. Aashish Kamat** as Independent Director w.e.f. close of business hours on December 17, 2026, upon completing the statutory maximum 8-year tenure.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers**\n* *No financial figures (revenue, EBITDA, PAT) are stated in this filing.*\n* **Tenure periods specified:**\n  * S. Ganesh Kumar Chairperson term: May 10, 2027 to April 29, 2029.\n  * Pradeep Natarajan re-appointment term: 3 years (June 1, 2027 to May 31, 2030).\n  * Aashish Kamat tenure: Completion of maximum 8 years permissible under Section 10A(2A) of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949.\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Outlook / Forward Statements**\n* The appointment of the Chairperson and re-appointment of the Executive Director remain subject to approval by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and other requisite regulatory/statutory approvals.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **RBI Approvals:** Track regulatory clearance from the RBI for both Mr. S. Ganesh Kumar\u2019s elevation to Chairperson and Mr. Pradeep Natarajan\u2019s second term as Executive Director.\n* No corporate action required by shareholders at this stage.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Neutral**: Routine corporate governance and advance succession planning with orderly board transitions well ahead of expiry dates."
  },
  {
   "s": "NETWEB",
   "n": "Netweb Technologies India Limited",
   "cat": "Outcome of Board Meeting",
   "when": "2026-10-24 16:26",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "Based on the regulatory filing for **Netweb Technologies India Limited** (Board Meeting Outcome dated **October 24, 2024**):\n\n---\n\n### 1. Most Important Fact\n* **Board Approval to Incorporate a Wholly Owned Subsidiary in Taiwan:** The Board approved the proposal to establish a 100% owned subsidiary in Taiwan to operate in the same industry.\n* **Capital Raise (QIP):** During the quarter, the company completed a Qualified Institutions Placement (QIP), raising **\u20b912,000.00 million** by issuing 2,505,219 equity shares at \u20b94,790 per share (face value \u20b92 + premium \u20b94,788).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Financial Numbers\n*(All figures in \u20b9 millions, except per-share data; periods ended September 30, 2024)*\n\n| Metric | Q2 FY25 (30-09-2024) | Q1 FY25 (30-06-2024) | Q2 FY24 (30-09-2023) | YoY (%) | QoQ (%) | H1 FY25 (30-09-2024) | H1 FY24 (30-09-2023) |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Revenue from operations** | 13,232.79 | 8,196.86 | 3,037.24 | +335.7% | +61.4% | 21,429.65 | 6,049.36 |\n| **Other income** | 128.62 | 84.72 | 9.24 | \u2014 | \u2014 | 161.13 | 19.77 |\n| **Total Income** | 13,361.41 | 8,281.58 | 3,046.48 | +338.6% | +61.3% | 21,590.78 | 6,069.13 |\n| **Total Expenses** | 11,534.92 | 7,140.20 | 2,626.22 | +339.2% | +61.5% | 18,622.91 | 5,232.81 |\n| **Finance Costs** | 238.00 | 115.24 | 9.30 | \u2014 | \u2014 | 353.24 | 19.08 |\n| **Profit Before Tax (PBT)** | 1,826.49 | 1,141.38 | 420.26 | +334.6% | +60.0% | 2,967.87 | 836.32 |\n| **Total Tax Expense** | 459.93 | 288.15 | 105.93 | \u2014 | \u2014 | 748.08 | 217.20 |\n| **Net Profit (PAT)** | **1,366.56** | **853.23** | **314.33** | **+334.8%** | **+60.2%** | **2,219.79** | **619.12** |\n| **Total Comprehensive Income** | 1,368.78 | 854.09 | 315.66 | +333.6% | +60.3% | 2,222.87 | 621.32 |\n| **Basic EPS (\u20b9)** | 23.54 | 14.98 | 5.55 | +324.1% | +57.1% | 38.60 | 10.93 |\n| **Diluted EPS (\u20b9)** | 23.54 | 14.98 | 5.55 | +324.1% | +57.1% | 38.60 | 10.93 |\n\n*(Note: EBITDA and operating margins are not separately stated as line items in the filing).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements\n* No formal quantitative forward revenue/margin guidance is provided in this filing.\n* **Subsidiary in Taiwan:** The company stated that the incorporation process has not yet been initiated; details regarding subscription cost and timing are to be determined upon approvals.\n* **ESOP Vesting:** 4,935 ESOPs granted on January 18, 2024, will vest over a period of 1\u20132 years (recorded ESOP cost of \u20b90.62 million for the half-year).\n\n---\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On\n* **Deployment of QIP Proceeds:** Monitor utilization of the \u20b912,000 million raised; as of September 30, 2024, \u20b93,500 million is held in Fixed Deposits, \u20b9587.88 million in a monitoring bank account, and \u20b9177.00 million in an escrow account.\n* **Working Capital & Inventory Build:** Inventories increased sharply to \u20b919,306.91 million (vs. \u20b98,048.44 million as of March 31, 2024), causing negative operating cash flow of \u20b9(6,391.48) million for H1 FY25.\n* **Taiwan Subsidiary Progress:** Track operational setup and strategic role (component sourcing/ODM partnerships) of the planned Taiwan entity.\n\n---\n\n### 5. One-Line Net Read\n**Highly Positive:** Exceptional top-line and net profit growth (>4x YoY and >60% QoQ), backed by a massive \u20b912,000 million equity injection strengthening the balance sheet for large AI/HPC server rollouts."
